D000:                          
D000:                                                                                 ; Applesoft BASIC was first written by
D000:                                                                                 ; Marc McDonald, the first employee of Microsoft,
D000:                                                                                 ; in mid-1976. That version was bought by Apple
D000:                                                                                 ; and released (on casette) in Nov. 1977.
D000:                          
D000:                                                                                 ; Version 2 was written by Randy Wigginton and
D000:                                                                                 ; others at Apple in spring 1978. This version
D000:                                                                                 ; was released in several different forms. The
D000:                                                                                 ; one reproduced by this source assembly file is
D000:                                                                                 ; the main-board ROM form, which appeared in the
D000:                                                                                 ; Apple ][ plus ROM at $D000-$F7FF.
D000:                          
